<report>
<line><title>Chi-square test (2 by k)</title></line>
<line></line>
<table>
<tr><th></th><th>Successes</th><th>Failures</th><th>Total</th><th>Per cent</th><th>Score</th></tr>
<block name="row">
<tr><td>Observed</td><td><in>obs_succ</in></td><td><in>obs_fail</in></td><td><in>obs_tot</in></td><td><in>obs_pc</in></td><td><in>score</in></td></tr>
<tr><td><model>Expected</model></td><td><model><in>exp_succ</in></model></td><td><model><in>exp_fail</in></model></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
</block><tr><th>Total</th><th><in>tot_succ</in></th><th><in>tot_fail</in></th><th><in>tot_tot</in></th><th><in>tot_pc</in></th></tr>
</table>
<block name="warn">
<line></line>
<line><warn>Warning: <in>num</in> out of <in>den</in> cells have expected frequency less than 5</warn></line>
</block>
<line></line>
<line>Total Chi&#xb2; = <in>chi</in>  |Chi| = <in>chi_abs</in> (<in>totdf</in> DF)  <pval><in>chi_p</in></pval></line>
<block name="z">
<line></line>
<line>Chi&#xb2; for linear trend = <in>chi_lin</in>  |Chi| = <in>chi_1df</in> (1 DF)  <pval><in>chi_lin_p</in></pval></line>
<line></line>
<line>Remaining Chi&#xb2; (non-linearity) = <in>chi_non</in> (<in>df</in> DF)  <pval><in>chi_non_p</in></pval></line>
</block>
</report>
